  "summary": "Six companion preprints dated 12–13 November 2026 document Euclid's first data release, covering survey status, validation and processing pipelines.",
  "synthesis": "The items form a coordinated documentation set for Euclid Data Release 1. The overview paper describes a two-part release of images, spectra and catalogues for about a billion objects from wide and deep fields, while the survey paper reports 2100 deg² of Wide Survey area. Supporting papers address data quality and processing: photometric masks tracing spatial variations in survey properties, multi-band photometry validated against the JWST-based COSMOS2025 catalogue (median offsets mostly within 10%, largest in NIR deep model-fitting), the PHZ pipeline using NNPZ nearest-neighbour inference from a COSMOS reference sample for galaxy properties, and NISP slitless spectroscopic redshifts validated against DESI DR1 with 98.5% redshift success. The new element is the quantified validation of DR1 products against external references. The items do not present cosmological results.",
